    "result_text": "I agree with the finding and addressed it. `AssignMemberId.hash8()` now routes through the shared `Hashing.sha256Hex(...)` primitive \u2014 the same one `OwnerIdentity` uses for the region-and-hash identity that HASH8 is required to match \u2014 with a `.substring(0, 8).toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT)`. This dropped the copied `MessageDigest` loop, the `NoSuchAlgorithmException` handling, and the `java.nio`/`java.security` imports, so every segment of the class now goes through a single-definition helper (`CityRegions`, `FiscalYear`, `Hashing`, `LuhnCheckDigit`, `OwnerTelephones`).\n\nThe output is identical (`memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` unchanged) and the acceptance suite is green.",
